O<peck_drill_z> sub
( Peck drilling along Z for lathe, with optional dwells )
( Call example: O<peck_drill_z> call [depth] [peck] [retract] [feed] [bottom_dwell] [retract_dwell] )
( #1 = total depth          e.g. -1.250   (negative Z) )
( #2 = peck increment       e.g. 0.100    (positive) )
( #3 = retract height       e.g. 0.050    (safe Z above start) )
( #4 = feed rate            e.g. 4.0      (units/min) )
( #5 = bottom dwell (sec)   e.g. 0.5      (optional, default 0) )
( #6 = retract dwell (sec)  e.g. 0.2      (optional, default 0) )

#<depth>       = #1
#<peck>        = #2
#<retract>     = #3
#<feed>        = #4
#<bottom_dwell> = [#5 ? 0]    (use 0 if not provided)
#<retract_dwell> = [#6 ? 0]

( Validation )
o<err> if [#<depth> GE 0]
  (debug, Depth must be negative!)
  M2
o<err> endif
o<err> if [#<peck> LE 0]
  (debug, Peck must be positive!)
  M2
o<err> endif

#<current_z> = #<_z>   (start from current Z, assumed to be retract/safe)

o<loop> while [#<current_z> GT #<depth>]
  #<next_z> = [#<current_z> - #<peck>]

  o<clamp> if [#<next_z> LT #<depth>]
    #<next_z> = #<depth>
  o<clamp> endif

  G1 Z#<next_z> F#<feed>          (feed to peck depth)

  G4 P#<bottom_dwell>             (dwell at bottom)

  G0 Z#<retract>                  (rapid retract)

  G4 P#<retract_dwell>            (dwell after retract)

  #<current_z> = #<next_z>
o<loop> endwhile

G0 Z#<retract>                    (final retract, redundant but safe)
M99                               (return)
O<peck_drill_z> endsub
